# Firmware archives and signatures are binary - never touch line endings.
*.zip   binary
*.sig   binary
*.if3   binary
*.nf3   binary

# Catalogue and tooling stay LF so hashes are stable across machines.
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Everything under content/ is hashed in the catalogue and compared byte for byte by iDM3,
# so git must not rewrite one of those bytes. The definition parts come out of IDM.config
# with CRLF, and normalising them to LF on commit changed each file after its digest had
# been taken - so every client rejected what it downloaded, correctly, and with no way to
# recover from the client side.
#
# Must stay below the rules above: in .gitattributes the last matching rule wins.
content/** -text
